# VEGA ARIES v2.0

## Overview

VEGA ARIES v2.0 is a RISC-V based development board developed by C-DAC. It is based on the THEJAS32 SoC and is designed for embedded systems and IoT applications.

In this project, the VEGA ARIES v2.0 can be used as an embedded controller for interfacing sensors and other peripherals of the firefighter safety system.

## Key Specifications

| Feature | Specification |
|---|---|
| Processor | VEGA ET1031 |
| SoC | THEJAS32 |
| Architecture | RISC-V |
| Clock Speed | 100 MHz |
| SRAM | 256 KB |
| Flash | 2 MB |
| UART | 3 |
| SPI | 4 |
| I2C | 3 |
| PWM | 8 |
| GPIO | 32 |
| I/O Voltage | 3.3 V |
| Input Voltage | 7–12 V |

## Role in the Project

The VEGA ARIES v2.0 provides an embedded platform for:

- Sensor interfacing
- UART communication
- SPI-based peripherals
- TFT/display interfacing
- Audio/alert control
- Real-time embedded control

## Why VEGA ARIES v2.0?

The board provides multiple communication interfaces and GPIOs in a compact embedded platform, making it suitable for wearable, sensor-fusion and IoT applications.

## Development

The board can be programmed using the Arduino IDE with the VEGA ARIES board support package. The official setup supports selecting:

`Tools → Board → VEGA Processor: ARIES Boards → ARIES v2`

## Project Integration

```text
Sensors / Radar
       ↓
VEGA ARIES v2.0
       ↓
